.TH KBLIGHT 1
.SH NAME
kblight \- the keyboard's light
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kblight
.RB [ off | low | high ]
.RI [ colour ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kblight
shows or sets the keyboard's light, through the USB server's port
.B kblight
(the Lenovo Legion's ITE 8258 keyboard); Settings does the same. Without
arguments it shows the level and the colour. With a level, it sets it;
with a colour only, the light takes that colour at the level it has (off:
high).
.I colour
is
.BR white ,
.BR red ,
.BR orange ,
.BR green ,
.BR cyan ,
.BR blue ,
.BR purple ,
or
.I RRGGBB
in hex.
.PP
The setting is kept and given to the keyboard again at each start.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0; 1 if there is no keyboard light, it did not take the setting, or for a
usage error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/kblight
The setting.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
kblight low cyan
kblight ff8000
kblight off
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR usb (4)
